---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout title="Refund Policy" heading="Refund Policy" description="Refund Policy for Public IPTV: first-purchase guarantee, renewal and multi-month rules, exclusions and how refunds are paid.">
  <p>
    Because every plan starts with a free trial, most problems surface before
    you pay anything. When something goes wrong on a paid plan, this policy
    explains exactly what happens. To claim, email contact@public-iptv.online
    with your account email, plan type and a description of the fault.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">1. First-purchase guarantee</h2>
  <p>
    If your first paid plan does not work on your devices and our support team
    cannot resolve it within a reasonable troubleshooting exchange, you are
    entitled to a full refund of that first payment when claimed within 7 days
    of the charge.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">2. Renewals</h2>
  <p>
    Monthly renewals are refundable in full if claimed within 48 hours of the
    renewal charge and the plan shows no material use since renewal. After that
    window, or once the month is substantially used, renewals are not
    refundable — but you can always cancel so no further charge occurs.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">3. Longer plans</h2>
  <p>
    Refunds on multi-month plans cover only the unused full months remaining at
    the time of the claim, and only where the service is at fault and
    unresolved by support. Used months and months already started are not
    refunded.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">4. Exclusions</h2>
  <p>
    No refund is due where the fault lies outside our service: your internet
    connection or Wi-Fi, an incompatible or misconfigured player app, VPN or DNS
    interference, or use beyond your plan's simultaneous-screen limit.
    Violations of the terms of service (for example credential sharing or
    restreaming) void refund eligibility.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">5. How refunds are paid</h2>
  <p>
    Approved refunds return to the original payment method within 10 business
    days of approval. Chargebacks filed while a good-faith claim is open may
    pause the review until the payment provider resolves the dispute.
  </p>
  <p>Last updated: 2026-10-04.</p>
</LegalLayout>
